  "evidence_rules": [
    "repo intelligence improves defaults and does not replace operator checks",
    "detected language packs record mixed-stack or monorepo shape without changing the primary default check",
    "quality signals record CI, test, docs, style, and package-manager evidence without granting authority",
    "standards sources record repo-local governance files without granting authority or marking checks passed",
    "standards source fingerprints record compact allowlisted file hashes without storing full content or reading secrets",
    "the worker context always begins with a repo intelligence contract, including generic repos, and the contract is advisory only",
    "bounded direct width starts real parallel candidate workers in isolated worktrees while preserving the primary run id and recording candidate run ids",
    "the worker context carries an execution geometry contract so single runs, bounded direct candidate workers, fleet streams, and fleet integration workers plan with the right coordination posture without gaining extra authority",
    "quality signals may enter the run context but must not grant authority or replace checks",
    "review axes may enter the run context as a principal-engineer self-review bar but must not mark work passed",
    "principal review gates record the cross-language quality bar without granting ship authority",
    "review packets expose repo intelligence and review axes without replaying event text",
    "principal review checklists are derived guidance and do not grant ship authority",
